-- Q1448: Audit Planning [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 320.09, performance materiality is set lower than overall materiality to reduce the probability that the aggregate of uncorrected and undetected misstatements exceeds materiality for the financial statements as a whole. This buffer accounts for misstatements that may go undetected across multiple accounts.
Wrong (A): Performance materiality is never equal to overall materiality; it must be set lower to provide the required buffer under AU-C 320.
Wrong (B): Performance materiality is set lower, not higher, than overall materiality. Setting it higher would defeat its purpose.
Wrong (D): The two concepts are directly related under AU-C 320; performance materiality is derived from overall materiality.$EXPL$
