-- Q1490: Risk Assessment [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 200.13, control risk is the risk that a material misstatement will not be prevented, or detected and corrected, on a timely basis by the entity''s internal control. It reflects the effectiveness of the entity''s control environment in addressing potential misstatements.
Wrong (A): This describes inherent risk, which is the susceptibility of an assertion to material misstatement due to the nature of the account balance, before considering controls.
Wrong (B): The risk that the auditor will issue an inappropriate opinion describes overall audit risk, not control risk specifically.
