UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 200.A42, detection risk is the risk that the auditor''s procedures will not detect a misstatement that exists and could be material. Unlike inherent and control risk, detection risk is directly controlled by the auditor through the nature, timing, and extent of audit procedures per AU-C 330.
Wrong (A): The existence of material misstatements in the financial statements relates to inherent risk and control risk, not detection risk.
Wrong (B): The failure of entity controls to prevent misstatements describes control risk, not detection risk.
